== Effect ==
* Grants one full Red [[Heart container]].
* {{Dlc|r}} Heals 1 additional {{e|Red Heart}}.

== Notes ==
* This item has a 12.6% chance to spawn from paying out a {{m|Beggar}} in addition to being in the [[Beggar (Item Pool)|Beggar item pool]]. Multiple copies can be obtained through this method.
* If the [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room Pool]] runs out of items, it will only contain Breakfast from that point onwards.
** Once other [[item pool]]s run out of items, they will only contain Treasure Room Pool items. This means that if the Treasure Room Pool was also exhausted, that item pool will only contain Breakfast.
*** {{dlc+|a}} With {{i|Chaos}}, every fully depleted item pool will only contain Breakfast.{{dlc-}}
** Breakfast spawned via exhausted item pools cannot be rerolled into other items with a few exceptions:
*** {{dlc+|a}} Rerolling Breakfast from an exhausted item pool while holding {{i|Chaos}} can reroll it into an item from another pool.{{dlc-}}
**** {{dlc+|r}} This also works with {{p|Soul of Eden}}.{{dlc-}}
*** {{dlc+|a}} Dropping {{t|NO!}} after exhausting an item pool while holding it will allow active items to spawn on pedestals again.{{dlc-}}
*** {{dlc|a+}} Having an item spawn from a non-exhausted pool before picking up Breakfast can allow rerolls to collected passive items (e.g. {{i|D4}}) to reroll Breakfast into an item from that item pool.{{dlc-}}
*** {{dlc+|r}} Losing {{i|Sacred Orb}} after exhausting an item pool while holding it will allow low quality items to appear again.{{dlc-}}

== Synergies ==
* {{i|Binge Eater}}: When Isaac picks up Breakfast it now grants: a permanent +0.2 [[Shot Speed]] and +2.5 [[Range]], a temporary +3.6 [[Damage]] (which diminishes to 0 in 30 seconds), heals 1 additional red heart, and takes a permanent -0.03 [[Speed]] reduction.

